From: SPIranha <https://github.com/MTSistemi/SPIranha>
Subject: [PATCH] fix the build with GCC 15 and newer

`enable_spi` is declared as `static void enable_spi()`, which in C23 means
"no parameters", but it is called once as `enable_spi(baud)`. GCC 15 rejects
that with "too many arguments to function 'enable_spi'".

This is not a behavioural change: `baud` is a global that the function already
reads by itself, and older compilers silently discarded the argument.

Applies to pico-serprog at commit 3ea792664ed29ca1ff3e2e78d1d16099684781bd.
---
diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index b06f92f..36a9265 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -322,7 +322,7 @@ int main() {
 	/* Setup USB */
 	tusb_init();
 	/* Setup PL022 SPI */
-	enable_spi(baud);
+	enable_spi();
 
 	command_loop();
 }
